  "id": "failure-modes-and-effects-analysis",
  "term": "failure modes and effects analysis",
  "definition": "Failure modes and effects analysis is a structured risk-assessment method used to identify possible points of failure in a process, estimate how likely and how serious their effects may be, and rank them so the most important risks can be addressed first. In the source, it is described as a way to evaluate hazards under uncertainty by combining ratings of probability and severity to prioritize failures.",
